WEBVTT

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:05.300
It shot!

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.200
It's huge!

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.520
Is that a landmine, too?

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:08.490
If it is...

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:10.280
Crap! It's heading right for...

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:15.970
Wha?! Why am I—?

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.120
Huh?

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.270
I'm in...

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.800
<b>Ogura Sio</b>

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:37.970
...Japan?

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:40.280
Come in.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.760
You're awake?

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.980
Saint-Germain!

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:52.180
Abilities of distinguished individuals, 
numerous throughout history,

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.400
have been stored in special E-genes.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:54.450
<b>E-genes</b>

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.080
The E-gene holders, 
who inherit those genes,

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.830
<b>AU balls</b>

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:03.820
summon the abilities sleeping 
within them via AU balls,

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:07.000
and embody AU weapons.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:13.170
The E-gene holders belonging to the 
supranational organization Dogoo

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:16.180
versus enemies from outer space 
known as Evolutionary Invasion Objects.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:19.530
This is the chronicle of their 
fateful battle for humanity!

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.060
Gun No. 9: Sio and Kaoru.

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:00.470
She's in Japan?!

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:05.740
Her injury isn't even that serious. 
Why'd they send her so far away?

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.980
Beats me. But apparently they did it on 
direct orders from the commander.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.170
I'm much more worried about Galileo.

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:23.220
Worst case scenario, 
she may never return to the front.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:29.990
Dammit.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.400
And what about us?

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.000
Vidocq is in talks with 
the higher-ups now.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.410
I guess it depends on the 
outcome of that.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.180
Man, we got screwed this time.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.510
Yeah, that battleship-class...

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:46.420
No.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:51.370
She was the only one who noticed...

00:03:56.130 --> 00:04:00.930
The combat engineer class. 
Its physical make-up is like an arthropod.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:04.060
This must be the class that 
dug that tunnel.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:08.580
The landmine class. 
Similarly arthropod-type.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.770
They explode on impact.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.080
It seems there are various sizes.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.990
The largest explosion is equivalent 
to a tactical nuke.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:24.430
And the battleship-class. It looks like its purpose 
is defending the tunnel.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:31.070
Its cephalopod body type seems optimal 
for patrolling deep inside.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:37.630
Despite us sending in a combined seven 
E-gene holders from the First and Second Platoons,

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:40.310
we were overwhelmed by just one 
battleship.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:44.960
Two were injured, and the <i>Clayton Forrester </i>
 was damaged— an utter defeat.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.820
Of course, the one who damaged the 
<i>Clayton Forrester</i> was Nobunagun...

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:55.390
But thanks to her, the many crew 
members were saved.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.900
Well, that's true.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:01.430
Nobunagun... She was one of the 
injured ones, wasn't she?

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:05.250
Yes, on the minor side.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:07.940
I'm glad the commander is safe, too.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:12.670
It's partially out of gratitude for that that you 
were sent to a hospital in your home country.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:14.960
So that's why.

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.210
Yes. Oh, by the way...

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:22.670
Your street clothes, and a gift from 
the commander: candied natto.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.920
Candied natto?

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.450
This whole thing?

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:29.240
The commander's favorite.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.400
Does it displease you in some way?

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.800
N-No! Not a bit, not a bit!

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.670
I thought not.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:42.300
Your injuries are but an abrasion of 
the head and a right ankle sprain.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:47.650
Tomorrow morning, you'll go back to the 
<i>Alex Logan</i>, so rest while you can today.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.640
Yessir...

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.400
Very well.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:00.630
So I'm in Japan.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:07.130
<b>Wangan Hospital</b>

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:05.100
Been a while since I've breathed 
in some Japanese air.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.130
I gotta get in touch with Mom.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:10.250
I'm in Japan, which means...

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.840
E-mail, e-mail!

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.690
<b>Sio!

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.640
These are all from Asao...

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:26.400
Hello? Door's open! C'mon in.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.320
Err... sorry.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:33.310
Sio! It's been so long!

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:36.520
I'm relieved. You look better than 
I thought you would.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.160
Asao!

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:46.080
You didn't know before 
I opened the door?

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.510
I don't get it.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:51.290
The battleship-class and its companions...

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:54.380
It's strange that they're all invertebrates.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:56.680
Yes, just as you say.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:58.610
The aim of the Evolutionary 
Invasion Objects...

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:02.420
...must be to lord over 
creation in humanity's place.

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:05.980
<b>Johnston Atoll, torpedo class </b>

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:07.920
It's for that reason they've been 
evolving as vertebrates up to now.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.030
<b>Hawaii, cruiser class</b>

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.860
<b>Bikini Atoll, cruiser class </b>

00:07:09.190 --> 00:07:11.860
However, this time it's bugs and squid.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:16.110
But there is no way Invasion Objects 
that had already evolved into fish

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:18.660
<b>Vertebrates </b>

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:18.660
<b>Invertebrates </b>

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:21.570
could go back the way they came 
and re-evolve into invertebrates.

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:25.960
In other words, it's possible they have 
a stock of their original cells—

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:31.870
yes, the cells that came to 
Earth on the meteorite—

00:07:31.870 --> 00:07:36.350
with which they evolve new Invasion Objects!

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.690
What makes you say that?

00:07:38.690 --> 00:07:39.800
Please observe.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.450
This is a diagram of the tunnel structure.

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:47.100
It's the data Galileo risked her life to get.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:50.480
In the bellies of the arthropods 
in the little rooms,

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:53.610
we detected Evolutionary 
Invasion Object cells.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:57.920
Since another type of Invasion Object 
is guarding these arthropods,

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:05.580
that must be mean they're protecting the cells 
inside their bodies and transporting them.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:09.210
The fact that they divide labor 
in an advanced way

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.750
was made clear in the 
<i>Musashi Wonder</i> incident.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.390
Just like ants or bees, huh.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:19.360
Yes. This is their nest...

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.240
A cell warehouse, a factory for new troops...

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:29.970
And the one protecting their eggs, 
their original cells, is the battleship.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.980
What? Is there something on my face?

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:45.170
What? N-No, nothing like that.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.890
It's just been a while, 
so I got kinda nervous.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:52.410
I freaked out when I heard. 
They said you were seriously injured.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:54.820
Don't worry. It's not so bad.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:56.830
Okay, that's good.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:59.690
But, our positions are 
reversed now, huh.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:01.000
Compared to?

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:05.770
Don't you remember? You came to see 
me when I was in the hospital.

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:06.930
Oh!

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:09.070
I was so happy.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:11.670
Your e-mails!

00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:12.520
Hm?

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:14.480
Thanks for e-mailing me.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:18.210
Sorry to bug you. You must've been 
too busy to read them.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:22.230
N-No, it's not like that! 
Dogoo is just really strict.

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:25.010
You can't use your phone anywhere!

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:31.380
So I only got your mails 
a bit ago, and... and...

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:36.830
I wrote you a ton, too, 
but I couldn't send them!

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:37.480
So!

00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:39.040
Aw, thanks.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:40.130
Huh?

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:44.800
You never responded, so I thought 
I was getting the cold shoulder.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.380
No way! I'd never...

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.010
That's fine, then, right?

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:52.770
Forget e-mail. Let's talk about 
everything right here, right now.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.240
Yeah! Let's!

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:01.300
We must capture this tunnel.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:06.710
If we can exterminate the original cells 
and prevent the appearance of new species,

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:10.800
we can limit their available 
strategies considerably.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.360
But to do that, we'd have to 
eliminate the battleship!

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:18.770
We can't beat that thing with just 
the First and Second Platoons.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:20.870
This is of a matter of utmost urgency!

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:24.840
We should gather all the active holders 
and focus them here.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:27.440
That we cannot do.

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:28.280
Why not?

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:31.320
Because we're in the thick of it, too.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:35.050
Multiple enemies detected off Tahiti!

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:38.530
This just in from Dai Zong, Third Platoon. 
The enemies on Hawaii have been defeated.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:44.940
Evolutionary Invasion Objects are currently 
making landfall in multiple areas in the Pacific.

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:50.080
It's obvious their multi-front invasion 
is to prevent us from massing an attack,

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:51.870
but we can't not deal with them.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:54.830
Report from a ship sailing in Tokyo Bay!

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:56.980
They've found the wake of what appears 
to be an Evolutionary Invasion Object!

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:59.560
Getting reinforcements is impossible.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:04.010
The troops we can put towards taking the tunnel 
are the First and Second Platoons only.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:06.790
Please strategize with that in mind.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.020
Understood.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:11.960
Everyone, please prioritize this operation.

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:12.910
Sir!

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:21.920
Shit.

00:11:25.590 --> 00:11:27.010
Are you sure that's what you saw?

00:11:27.430 --> 00:11:28.990
I'm tellin' ya, no doubt about it.

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:31.050
Then where is it?

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:32.640
That's the weird thing...

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.410
Are you sure it wasn't just 
some trash or something?

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:39.340
This is Tokyo Bay! How could there be 
an Evolutionary Invasion Object here?

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:43.510
Yeah, you're right...

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:01.840
And so, well, there are a lot of issues, 
but at least everybody else is nice to me.

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:05.650
Just Adam— err, Jack the Ripper—

00:12:05.650 --> 00:12:08.290
He picks on me for everything!

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:09.380
Aww.

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:14.400
In the first place, isn't Jack the Ripper 
just a criminal? He slices people up!

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:19.170
Sio, it seems like maybe you 
have a thing for him?

00:12:19.170 --> 00:12:21.240
Huh? Whaaat?!

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:26.750
Well, you've been talking about Jack the Ripper 
way more than Newton or Gandhi.

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:29.780
It's n-nothing like that! 
No way, no way!

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:34.030
But, Sio, you're so amazing.

00:12:34.030 --> 00:12:35.470
What do you mean?

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:37.890
It's gotten, well, pretty rough 
around here, too.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:46.350
Because of all the Evolutionary Invasion Objects, 
there are people fleeing the coast and buying up food.

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:48.110
That bad, huh?

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:51.540
And in any hospital— oh, see?

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:55.100
Japan is still way safer than some places,

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:59.210
so victims from other countries 
are being brought here.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:04.440
You're fighting to decrease the number 
of sufferers, if even by a little.

00:13:04.780 --> 00:13:06.110
That's why you're amazing.

00:13:06.110 --> 00:13:09.460
But none of that is on my mind at all. 
I just go into a trance, and...

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:15.570
And when it's over, I always worry 
about whether I even did okay.

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:17.690
I'm not amazing at all.

00:13:17.690 --> 00:13:19.750
No, you are!

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:24.200
That's why... well, it's nothing 
compared to you... but, look!

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:27.240
<b>[Required] Nurse: National Exam Workbook</b>

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.480
You're gonna be a nurse?

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:30.970
I'm even already volunteering on my 
days off at a nearby hospital.

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:35.100
Compared to you it's not much, 
but I thought I could fight in my own way.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:39.710
You as a nurse? Wow! 
Just like Florence Nightingale.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.050
That's going a bit far!

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.260
<b>Evolutionary Invasion Object Warning</b>

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:46.330
An Evolutionary Invasion Object warning!

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:47.340
What?

00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:56.380
Now over Odaiba.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:59.930
One landing ship and multiple 
infantry confirmed!

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:01.920
<b>Yokohama </b>

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:03.940
<b>Makuhari </b>

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.110
<b>Evolutionary Invasion Object Warning: 
Please take shelter immediately.</b>

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:07.900
There's an evacuation order for the 
area along the coast of Tokyo Bay!

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:07.900
<b>See damage report</b>

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:10.670
Please follow staff instructions 
and take shelter!

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.260
Asao, I have to go!

00:14:14.970 --> 00:14:17.570
Ow! Owww....

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:20.090
Don't overdo it, Sio.

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:22.570
I'll be okay. I can make
 it on my own...

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:25.590
Oh... right. I don't have my AU ball.

00:14:25.970 --> 00:14:27.480
Here, hold on.

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:29.150
Uh... okay.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:42.610
Are you okay? Let's all board in order.

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:49.370
Sio, wait here for just a minute.

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:53.750
I'm gonna go help for a bit. 
But I mean it! Don't go anywhere.

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:56.620
Let me help you!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:57.790
Thanks!

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:04.510
Hello? Secret call! 1248751.

00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:06.800
This is Ogura Sio: codename, Nobunagun!

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:09.700
Please hurry! Get me 
someone on the<i> Alex Logan</i>!

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:16.920
Yes! Please request Dogoo action! 
At this rate...

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:29.400
That's right! Please drop 
an AU ball— it's urgent!

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:34.750
Our positions really have reversed.

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:38.760
I can't do anything if I don't 
have an AU ball...

00:15:44.070 --> 00:15:45.430
Asao, run!

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.330
This is the last one, right?

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:48.150
Thank you.

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:49.550
Asao!!

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:54.760
Asao!

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:08.660
Saint-Germain?

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:19.200
Well, this won't do.

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:24.920
I've gone and damaged the car Dogoo purchased 
for me, despite our low budget.

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:50.190
N-No way...

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.470
This can't be...

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.560
Go!

00:16:58.560 --> 00:16:59.130
Huh?

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:00.370
Now!

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:02.100
But...

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:03.100
Just go!

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:05.290
Over here!

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:10.230
Hey, this way! I'm the one you're after!

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:13.930
Asao, that's insane! 
You gotta get outta here!

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:18.040
That's it! Over here!

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:22.100
Sio, run while I distract it!

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:23.280
Asao!

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:25.010
Oww!

00:17:28.760 --> 00:17:33.500
Just like that. Good boy. C'mere.

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:39.940
Argh... I can't just wait 
around for an AU ball.

00:17:40.190 --> 00:17:43.260
I'll protect Asao!

00:17:45.510 --> 00:17:47.470
Oda Nobunaga...

00:17:47.470 --> 00:17:54.590
If your soul really is living inside of me,
lend me your strength!

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:09.130
It can't be helped!

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.480
Did I just...?

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:28.500
Sio!

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:31.580
What just happened? 
How'd you do that?

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:34.870
Hm? I... don't really know.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:37.080
You really are amazing, Sio!

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:42.800
But I think I'm all out of energy...

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:44.000
Sio!

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:54.290
Ahh... this is too much for me.

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:55.760
Sio!

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:12.360
What's that?

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.050
The drop pod...

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:22.790
Well, now... this is a perfect mess.

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:25.670
Huh? What's wrong?

00:19:27.700 --> 00:19:28.920
Y-You're late!

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:33.710
Hey, now! Is that what you say to 
the guy who came to save you?

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:39.270
Well, whatever. Why don't 
you just take a nap?

00:19:46.310 --> 00:19:47.650
C'mon...

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:52.000
Why ya actin' so tough, Lil' Fishie?

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:58.060
Phew.

00:19:58.190 --> 00:19:59.680
Ah! Sio!

00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:10.520
<b>Emergency brief: Damage along the coast of Tokyo Bay 
caused by Evolutionary Invasion Objects...</b>

00:20:06.420 --> 00:20:10.520
The Evolutionary Invasion Objects that 
damaged multiple areas along the coast of Tokyo Bay

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:13.530
were brought under control by 
Dogoo's Fourth Platoon.

00:20:12.570 --> 00:20:13.800
Are you up?

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:16.950
The accompanying regulations on the 
Bayshore Route of the Shuto Expressway...

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:16.950
Good.

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:20.450
Man, you really did 
save me this time.

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.460
No way. It was all you.

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:25.700
Nuh-uh. If you hadn't been there, I'd be...

00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:28.310
Then I guess we're even?

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:32.580
Saving and being saved... 
Switching now and then isn't so bad, right?

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:33.370
But...

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:35.150
That's what friends are for!

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:38.420
Right!

00:20:38.850 --> 00:20:42.370
Ah... friendship is a beautiful thing.

00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:45.940
Huh? Well, yeah, 
she's really important to m—

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:51.840
U-Uh... S-Saint-Germain... 
H-H-How...?

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:55.420
Hmm. It seems my current constitution 
displeases you.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.930
W-Whadaya mean, "constitution"?

00:20:58.180 --> 00:21:01.210
More importantly, it's back 
to your platoon tomorrow.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:03.690
There's no time to waste in 
carrying out this operation.

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:06.730
Hm? Operation?

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:07.530
I'm going.

00:21:09.340 --> 00:21:10.390
Hey, hey.

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:14.280
That guy must be Jack, right?

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:17.360
Huh? Err, yeah.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.910
I think you guys seem 
like a good match.

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:28.760
See you later!

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:30.530
Hm? You're leaving?

00:21:30.900 --> 00:21:34.050
Yeah. Take it easy. 
I'll come again.

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:36.370
Okay.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:40.010
You done jabbering?

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:44.460
Y-Y-Yes.

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:47.350
Then it's my turn.

00:21:47.350 --> 00:21:48.070
Huh?

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:51.550
I have something I need 
to talk to you about.

00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:29.020
Up and at 'em, m'lady.

00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:31.670
"M'lady?" What's with the 
personality switch?

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:33.700
Excuse me. An old habit.

00:23:33.700 --> 00:23:35.180
Saint-Germain, your past was...?

00:23:35.180 --> 00:23:37.630
Next time, Gun No. 10: Dogoo!

00:23:37.630 --> 00:23:40.020
Argh! Don't change the subject!
